Summary:
During today’s session, the focus was on revising core React concepts and applying them to enhance the existing features of the Developer Portfolio Evaluator application. Key topics such as state management, component structure, and event handling were reviewed and better understood. These concepts were then used to refine parts of the frontend for improved efficiency and maintainability. Minor feature improvements were implemented to make the application more responsive and user-friendly.

Outcomes:
By the end of the session, there was a clearer understanding of React fundamentals and their practical application in the project. The frontend became more structured and easier to manage due to better use of components and state. Improvements made to features resulted in smoother user interactions and cleaner code organization. Overall, the session strengthened both conceptual knowledge and practical implementation in the project.
